event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1450,"item_id":"fc_02f8293d92061092016adb4e0fb37c81918c8edab638e9140a","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"header\":\"import Mathlib\\nopen scoped TensorProduct\\nnoncomputable def dividedPower (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] (f : V →ₗ[ℂ] V) (r : ℕ) : V →ₗ[ℂ] V := ((Nat.factorial r : ℂ)⁻¹) • (f ^ r)\\nnoncomputable def tensorAction {K : Type*} [Field K] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] (f : M →ₗ[ℤ] M) : K ⊗[ℤ] M →ₗ[K] K ⊗[ℤ] M := TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K f\\ndef InvariantUnder (K : Type*) [Field K] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module K E] (f : E →ₗ[K] E) (W : Submodule K E) : Prop := ∀ z ∈ W, f z ∈ W\\ndef LieIrreducible (K : Type*) [Field K] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module K E] (x y z : E →ₗ[K] E) : Prop := Nontrivial E ∧ ∀ W : Submodule K E, InvariantUnder K E x W → InvariantUnder K E y W → InvariantUnder K E z W → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\\nstructure LieLatticeData (lam : ℤ) (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] where\\n  V : Type\\n  [vAdd : AddCommGroup V]\\n  [vMod : Module ℂ V]\\n  basisV : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℂ V\\n  basisM : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℤ M\\n  embed : M →ₗ[ℤ] V\\n  x : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  y : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  z : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  xM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  yM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  zM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  v : V\\ndef LieLatticeData.H004 {lam : ℤ} {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] (D : LieLatticeData lam M) : Prop := by\\n  letI := D.vAdd\\n  letI := D.vMod\\n  exact (∀ i, D.basisV i = D.embed (D.basisM i)) ∧ Function.Injective D.embed ∧\\n    (∀ w, D.z (D.x w) - D.x (D.z w) = (2:ℂ) • D.x w) ∧\\n    (∀ w, D.z (D.y w) - D.y (D.z w) = (-2:ℂ) • D.y w) ∧\\n    (∀ w, D.x (D.y w) - D.y (D.x w) = D.z w) ∧ D.v ≠ 0 ∧ D.x D.v = 0 ∧ D.z D.v = (lam:ℂ) • D.v ∧\\n    (∀ m, D.embed (D.xM m) = D.x (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.yM m) = D.y (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    (∀ m, D.embed (D.zM m) = D.z (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.x r (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.y r (D.embed m)) ∧\\n    LieIrreducible ℂ D.V D.x D.y D.z\\n\",\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"K\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instK\",\"type\":\"Field K\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"p\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"lam\",\"type\":\"ℤ\"},{\"name\":\"M\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instM\",\"type\":\"AddCommGroup M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"instModM\",\"type\":\"Module ℤ M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"D\",\"type\":\"LieLatticeData lam M\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"Nat.Prime p\",\"H002\":\"CharP K p\",\"H003\":\"(0 : ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p : ℤ)\",\"H004\":\"D.H004\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"LieIrreducible K (K ⊗[ℤ] M) (tensorAction D.xM) (tensorAction D.yM) (tensorAction D.zM)\",\"representation\":\"The arbitrary free lattice is M with a Z-basis and an injective inclusion into the complex highest-weight module V. The data record carries the actual complex operators and their integral restrictions. Scalar extension is represented by K tensor_Z M, with K acting on the first factor; this is related to the source ordering M tensor_Z K by the tensor commutor, which must be proved/used as a conversion. The target predicate means nonzero and every K-subspace invariant under all three induced actions is zero or the whole space. This is not a standard-lattice specialization.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"T001\",\"statement\":\"LieIrreducible K (K ⊗[ℤ] M) (tensorAction D.xM) (tensorAction D.yM) (tensorAction D.zM)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S001\",\"S002\",\"S003\",\"S004\",\"S005\",\"S006\",\"S007\",\"S008\"],\"explanation\":\"Single assembled obligation preserving the NL0 route: establish the divided-power basis and termination (S001), construct and preserve matrix units including the composite coefficient computation and p=2/lambda=0 cases (S002), analyze the arbitrary lattice coordinate modules and rank-one generator without presupposing freeness (S003), reduce via the arbitrary lattice basis to M tensor K and transport x,y,h (S004), show matrix units survive since r! and binomial coefficients are units for lambda<p (S005), extract a nonzero coordinate from a nonzero invariant subspace (S006), use E_{j,i} and invert the nonzero coordinate to obtain every basis vector (S007), and conclude nonzero irreducibility by the zero/nonzero case split (S008). This single node is intentionally a coarse source boundary; its implementation will need local elaboration into checked sublemmas without altering the given source assumptions.\"}],\"terminal\":\"T001\",\"source_outputs\":{\"P\":\"T001\"}}}"}

